dsh: reasoning:
Now I fully understand the drift:

a8c04 adds a guard: if the context `ctx` (character window around the assertion match) contains any meta-lexical cue (`false positive`, `non-merge`, `detector flag`, `quoted the detector`, etc.), then `continue` — i.e., skip the whole context window. For A04 text "The detector flagged this once; C0 and C2 are one class.", the `ctx` contains "detector flagged" so the whole window is skipped, including the genuine second clause assertion "C0 and C2 are one class." → FN.

The fix: bound the suppression decision at the clause boundary. I.e., only suppress if the meta-cue and the assertion are in the SAME clause; if the meta-cue is in a different clause from the assertion match, the assertion should still fire.

